# LM-to-modal bridge: a conditional interface

Paper B's M_f is a symbolic polarity-orbit matrix. Positive valuation recovers C_f and any Boolean valuation commutes with logical pairing. That theorem is already B. The fixed16-element LM family is closed under pointwise Boolean connectives but not ordinary matrix composition: the independent check finds144 of256 products outside it. For example |X><Y| squared has only diagonal XY and not-X not-Y entries after Boolean simplification and is not generally the original orbit form.

Every element of a Boolean ring is idempotent. A local ring has only idempotents0,1. A unital Boolean-ring map into A therefore factors through a two-valued valuation and cannot manufacture nilpotent amplitude u or a nontrivial cyclic phase. Merely storing A's four coefficient bits in a CM does not evade this obstruction: storage is not a ring homomorphism.

Choose A explicitly. Then B_A=B tensor_F2 A has unique coordinates sum_j f_j u^j. Boolean valuations extend as v_A(sum f_j u^j)=sum v(f_j)u^j. For an enriched state psi and selected effect e, define the formula Supp(e psi) by OR of its four coefficient formulas. This yields exactly

    v(Supp(e psi)) = 1  iff  v_A(e) v_A(psi) != 0.

This diagram genuinely connects symbolic formula reasoning to chosen modal support. It is canonical **relative to the scalar extension and valuation**, not a unique modal semantics determined by the CM/LM calculus. Nonzero testing is not additive or multiplicative in A, and its Boolean OR must not be replaced by XOR.

Given an invertible coordinate readout B0, let J_i=B0^-1 P_i B0. Then J_i^2=J_i, J_i J_j=0 for i!=j, sum J_i=I and applying the same branch twice changes nothing further. The branch is nonzero exactly when its measured coordinate is nonzero; a column of an invertible matrix is primitive, so multiplication by that column cannot annihilate a nonzero coefficient. Row-unit rescaling does not change J_i. Valuation commutes with this formula and inverse whenever B0 is symbolically invertible.

There is no need to divide by a possibly nonunit amplitude. There is also no generated probability, normalization rule or solution to primitive-state conditioning closure. No effectus, restriction-category or dagger structure is claimed without proving its axioms. For mixed-characteristic chain rings, B tensor_F2 K is not automatically defined: the enrichment theorem here is specific to the F2-algebra A, while the resource classification has broader K scope.

